```
HAL_EXTI_SetConfigLine() produces a Hard-Fault

### Reason:

```
HAL_StatusTypeDef HAL_EXTI_SetConfigLine(EXTI_HandleTypeDef *hexti, EXTI_ConfigTypeDef *pExtiConfig)
{
  uint32_t regval; // temporary variable to calculate peripheral address is a integer type not a pointer

// ...
// EXTI_MODE_INTERRUPT = 1
regval = (uint32_t)EXTI_BASE;
regval += pExtiConfig->Mode; // >> leads to odd number
*(__IO uint32_t *) regval |= pExtiConfig->Line; // illegal access for peripherals and wrong address for mode

//...
}
```

- Same problem for trigger rising or falling edge -> additional wrong base address for RTSR, FTSR

- Register EXTI-IMR is cleared but not set again by  HAL_EXTI_SetConfigLine() >> no interrupt

